    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's what I changed and why it stays low-impact.\n\n## Changes (2 files)\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 replaced the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` per-city-sequence scheme with the new region-and-hash identity:\n- `REGION` = region derived from the postcode (reusing the existing `Locality.of(postcode, city)`).\n- `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)` \u2014 4 digest bytes formatted with `%02X`.\n- Dropped the sequence entirely, so the function no longer needs the `OwnerRepository` lookup.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line: `locality` now derives from the new identity (the `REGION` segment before the `-` in `customerCode`), with a null-safe fallback to the old postcode/city derivation for records that predate a code.\n\n## What followed automatically\n- **Membership number** (`MembershipNumber.of(customerCode, \u2026)`) and its **check digit** (`CheckDigit.of(customerCode)`) already take `customerCode` as input, so they now compute over `NSW-16E6609E`-style codes with no edit.\n- The **create audit record** (`SaveOwner`) already logs `customerCode`, so it now emits the new value (confirmed in the run: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E \u2026`).\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\nOnly 2 files touched. Each changed method is small and cohesive: `service` stays at CC\u22481, the SHA logic lives in a tiny private `hash8` helper rather than bloating `service`, and no surrounding class complexity grew. The mapper edit is a single expression line. Because membership number, check digit, and the audit line already sourced from `customerCode`, redefining `customerCode` propagated the new identity everywhere without editing those classes.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
